<%--
Rsx_Default_Spinner

The framework's stock spinner: a small rotating circle, drawn at a FIXED size and centered
both ways in whatever box its host provides. The host owns the box and is a centering
stage, never a scale target - a loading region may be an entire panel or form, and a
spinner that filled one would be a rotating shape the size of the region.

Drawn in currentColor so it is legible on any surface: core has no palette, and the
spinner inherits the colour of whatever the host is sitting in. The arc is inlined so core
depends on no icon component.

Applications replace it by registering their own component with Rsx.set_default_spinner()
from a static on_app_modules_define() - the first boot phase. The first SPA page renders
(and draws its spinners) before app_init and app_ready, so a registration made in either
of those is not in force for that page.
--%>
<Define:Rsx_Default_Spinner tag="div">
    <svg class="Rsx_Default_Spinner__icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
         viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
         stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-6.219-8.56"/>
    </svg>
</Define:Rsx_Default_Spinner>
